   518	Find a specific checkpoint
   519	You can filter the state history to find checkpoints matching specific criteria:
   520	
   521	```
   522	history = list(graph.get_state_history(config))
   523	
   524	# Find the checkpoint before a specific node executed
   525	before_node_b = next(s for s in history if s.next == ("node_b",))
   526	
   527	# Find a checkpoint by step number
   528	step_2 = next(s for s in history if s.metadata["step"] == 2)
   529	
   530	# Find checkpoints created by update_state
   531	forks = [s for s in history if s.metadata["source"] == "update"]
   532	
   533	# Find the checkpoint where an interrupt occurred
   534	interrupted = next(
   535	    s for s in history
   536	    if s.tasks and any(t.interrupts for t in s.tasks)
   537	)
   538	
   539	```
